          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
            %em Moonshine
            refers to mysterious connections between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Monster+simple+group"} Monster simple group
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+function"} modular function
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/j-invariant"} j-invariant
          %p
            There were a bunch of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjectures"} conjectures
            about this connection that were proved by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Borcherds"} Richard Borcherds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moonshine+vertex+algebra"} Moonshine vertex algebra
            (constructed then later in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#FrenkelLepowskiMeurman89"} FLM 89
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simple+groups"} simple groups
          %p
            The whole idea of moonshine began with
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+McKay"} John McKay
            = succeed "\u2019s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Monster+group"} Monster group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+representation"} irreducible representation
            has
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            196883, and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/j-invariant"} j-invariant
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j(\tau)
            has the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+series"} Fourier series
            expansion
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi q
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %mn 744
                  %mo +
                  %mn 196884
                  %mi q
                  %mo +
                  %mn 21493760
                  %msup
                    %mi q
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %mi …
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  j(\tau) = q^{-1} + 744 + 196884q + 21493760q^{2} + \dots
          %p
            where
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                    %mo =
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mn 2
                    %mi π
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q=\exp(i2\pi\tau)
          %p
            But the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Monster+group"} Monster group
            was merely
            %em conjectured
            to exist until Griess (1982) explicitly constructed it. The construction is horribly complicated (take the sum of three irreducible representations for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/centralizer"} centralizer
            of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/involution"} involution
            of…).
          %p
            %a{:href => "#FrenkelLepowskiMeurman89"} Frenkel-Lepowski-Meurman 89
            constructed an infinite-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            for the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Monster+vertex+algebra"} Monster vertex algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kac-Moody+algebra"} Kac-Moody algebra
            via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+string+theory"} bosonic string theory
            and the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Goddard-Thorn+theorem"} Goddard-Thorn "No Ghost" theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Monster+group"} Monster group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+action"} acts
            naturally on this “Moonshine Module” (denoted by
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ♮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V\natural
          %p
            To cut the story short, we end up getting from the Monster group to a module it acts on which is related to “modular stuff” (namely, the modular
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/j-invariant"} j-invariant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Terry+Gannon"} Terry Gannon
            pitches is that Moonshine is a generalization of this association, it’s a sort of “mapping” from “Algebraic gadgets” to “Modular stuff”.
          %h2#AutomorphismGroupsOfVertexOperatorAlgebras Automorphism groups of vertex operator algebras
          %p
            Realizations of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sporadic+finite+simple+groups"} sporadic finite simple groups
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+of+a+vertex+operator+algebra"} automorphism groups of vertex operator algebras
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+string+theory"} type II string theory
            (mostly on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3-surfaces"} K3-surfaces
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HET+-+II+duality"} HET - II duality
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Conway+group"} Conway group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Co
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Co_{0}
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} group of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphisms+of+a+super+VOA"} automorphisms of a super VOA
                of the unique chiral
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+of+supersymmetries"} N=1
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vertex+operator+algebra"} super vertex operator algebra
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/central+charge"} central charge
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo =
                      %mn 12
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c = 12
                without fields of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+weight"} conformal weight
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1/2
              %p
                (
                %a{:href => "#Duncan05"}> Duncan 05
                , see also
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "#PaquettePerssonVolpato17"} Paquette-Persson-Volpato 17, p. 9
            %li
              %p
                similarly, there is a super VOA, the
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Monster+vertex+operator+algebra"} Monster vertex operator algebra
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} group of
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphisms+of+a+VOA"} automorphisms of a VOA
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monster+group"} monster group
              %p
                (
                %a{:href => "#FrenkelLepowskiMeurman89"}> Frenkel-Lepowski-Meurman 89
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "#GriessLam11"} Griess-Lam 11
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Monster"} Monster
            %li
              %p moonshine
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mathieu+moonshine"} Mathieu moonshine
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/umbral+moonshine"} umbral moonshine
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/O%27Nan+moonshine"} O'Nan moonshine
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+of+a+vertex+operator+algebra"} automorphism of a vertex operator algebra
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Borcherds"}> Richard Borcherds
                ,
                %em What is Moonshine?,
              %p
                Proceedings of the International Congress of Mathematicians, Vol. I (Berlin, 1998).
                %em Doc. Math.
                1998, Extra Vol. I, 607–615 (electronic).
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=1660657"} MR1660657
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9809110"} arXiv:math/9809110v1
                [math.QA]
            %li
              %p
                John F. R. Duncan, Michael J. Griffin, Ken Ono,
                %em Moonshine
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1411.6571"}> arXiv:1411.6571
                )
            %li#GriessLam11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Griess"} Robert Griess
                Jr., Ching Hung Lam,
                %em A new existence proof of the Monster by VOA theory
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1103.1414"}> arXiv:1103.1414
                )
            %li#FrenkelLepowskiMeurman89
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Frenkel"}> Igor Frenkel
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Lepowsky"} James Lepowsky
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Vertex operator algebras and the monster
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 134
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=996026"} MR0996026
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Terry+Gannon"}> Terry Gannon
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Monstrous moonshine: the first twenty-five years
                %em Bull. London Math. Soc.
                %strong 38
                (2006), no. 1, 1–33.
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2201600"} MR2201600
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0402345"} arXiv:math/0402345
                [math.QA]
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Terry+Gannon"}> Terry Gannon
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Moonshine beyond the Monster: The Bridge Connecting Algebra, Modular Forms and Physics
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2257727"} MR2257727
            %li
              %p
                Koichiro Harada,
                = succeed "." do
                  %em “Moonshine” of finite groups
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2722318"} MR2722318
            %li
              %p
                Griess, Robert L., Jr.; Lam, Ching Hung
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A moonshine path from E8 to the Monster
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2747229"} MR2747229
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0910.2057v2"} arXiv:0910.2057v2
                [math.GR]
            %li
              %p
                Jae-Hyun Yang “Kac-Moody algebras, the Monstrous Moonshine, Jacobi forms and infinite products.”
                %em Number theory, geometry and related topics
                (Iksan City, 1995), 13–82, Pyungsan Inst. Math. Sci., Seoul, 1996.
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=1404967"} MR1404967
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0612474"} arXiv:math/0612474v2
                [math.NT]
            %li
              %p
                Vassilis Anagiannis,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Miranda+Cheng"} Miranda Cheng
                %em TASI Lectures on Moonshine
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1807.00723"}> arXiv:1807.00723
                )
          %h3#historical_references Historical References
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Conway"} John Conway
                and Simon Norton, “Monstrous moonshine.”
                %em Bull. London Math. Soc.
                %strong 11
                (1979), no. 3, 308–339;
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=554399"} MR0554399
                (81j:20028)
            %li#FrenkelLepowskiMeurman89
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Frenkel"}> Igor Frenkel
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Lepowsky"} James Lepowsky
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                as character.”
                %em Proc. Nat. Acad. Sci. U.S.A.
                %strong 81
                (1984), no. 10, Phys. Sci., 3256–3260.
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=747596"} MR0747596
                (85e:20018)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Griess"}> Robert Griess
                , “The friendly giant.”
                %em Invent. Math.
                %strong 69
                (1982), no. 1, 1–102.
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=671653"} MR671653
                (84m:20024)
            %li
              %p
                John G. Thompson, “Some numerology between the Fischer-Griess Monster and the elliptic modular function.”
                %em Bull. London Math. Soc.
                %strong 11
                (1979), no. 3, 352–353.
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=554402"} MR0554402
                (81j:20030)
          %h3#FurtherDevelomentsReferences Further developments
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Miranda+Cheng"}> Miranda Cheng
                , John F. R. Duncan, Jeffrey A. Harvey,
                %em Umbral Moonshine
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1204.2779"}> arXiv:1204.2779
                )
            %li
              %p
                John F. R. Duncan, Michael J. Griffin and Ken Ono,
                %em Proof of the Umbral Moonshine Conjecture
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1503.01472"}> arXiv:1503.01472
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Scott+Carnahan"}> Scott Carnahan
                ,
                %em Monstrous Moonshine over Z?
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1804.04161"}> arXiv:1804.04161
                )
          %p
            Possible relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+cohomology"} elliptic cohomology
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+modular+forms"}> topological modular forms
            ):
          %ul
            %li
              Jan Albert,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Justin+Kaidi"} Justin Kaidi
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ying-Hsuan+Lin"} Ying-Hsuan Lin
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topological modularity of Supermoonshine
              %strong 2023
              3 (2023) 033B06 [
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.14923"}> arXiv:2210.14923
              ,
              = succeed "]" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1093/ptep/ptad034"} doi:10.1093/ptep/ptad034
          %h3#realization_in_superstring_theory Realization in superstring theory
          %p
            Discussion of possible realizations in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring+theory"} superstring theory
            (specifically
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+string+theory"} type II string theory
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3-surfaces"} K3-surfaces
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HET+-+II"} HET - II
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphisms+of+super+vertex+operator+algebras"} automorphisms of super vertex operator algebras
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                S. Chaudhuri, D.A. Lowe,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Monstrous String-String Duality
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9512226"} arXiv:hep-th/9512226
            %li#Duncan05
              %p
                John F. Duncan,
                %em Super-moonshine for Conway’s largest sporadic group
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0502267"}> arXiv:math/0502267
                )
            %li#PaquettePerssonVolpato16
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Natalie+Paquette"}> Natalie Paquette
                , Daniel Persson, Roberto Volpato,
                %em Monstrous BPS-Algebras and the Superstring Origin of Moonshine
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1601.05412"}> arXiv:1601.05412
                )
            %li#KachruPaquetteVolpato16
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shamit+Kachru"}> Shamit Kachru
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Natalie+Paquette"} Natalie Paquette
                %em 3D String Theory and Umbral Moonshine
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1603.07330"}> arXiv:1603.07330
                )
            %li#PaquettePerssonVolpato17
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Natalie+Paquette"}> Natalie Paquette
                , Daniel Persson, Roberto Volpato,
                %em BPS Algebras, Genus Zero, and the Heterotic Monster
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1701.05169"}> arXiv:1701.05169
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shamit+Kachru"}> Shamit Kachru
                , Arnav Tripathy,
                %em The hidden symmetry of the heterotic string
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1702.02572"}> arXiv:1702.02572
                )
          %p
            Specifically in relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactifications"} KK-compactifications
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3-surfaces"} K3-surfaces
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+heterotic+and+type+II+string+theory"}> duality between heterotic and type II string theory
            )
          %ul
            %li#ChengHarrisonVolpatoZimet16
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Miranda+Cheng"}> Miranda Cheng
              , Sarah M. Harrison, Roberto Volpato, Max Zimet,
              %em K3 String Theory, Lattices and Moonshine
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1612.04404"}> arXiv:1612.04404
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s40687-018-0150-4"} doi:10.1007/s40687-018-0150-4
          %p
            Possible relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+M-theory"} bosonic M-theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alessio+Marrani"}> Alessio Marrani
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Rios"} Michael Rios
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Chester"} David Chester
              = succeed "," do
                %em Monstrous M-theory
              %strong 15
              2 (2023) 490; &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.3390/sym15020490"}> doi:10.3390/sym15020490
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2008.06742"} arXiv:2008.06742
          %p
            Relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Seiberg-Witten+theory"} Seiberg-Witten theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Shun’ya Mizoguchi,
                %em Seiberg-Witten Theory and Monstrous Moonshine
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2208.10301"}> arXiv:2208.10301
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Shun’ya Mizoguchi, Takumi Oikawa, Hitomi Tashiro, Shotaro Yata,
                %em More on Seiberg-Witten Theory and Monstrous Moonshine
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.07251"}> arXiv:2211.07251
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Roberta Angius, Stefano Giaccari, Sarah M. Harrison, Roberto Volpato:
              %em Non-invertible defects from the Conway SCFT to K3 sigma models I: general results
              \&amp;lbrack;
